  "chain_ok": true,
  "message": "All tests pass now (2 of 2).\n\nThe bug was in `src/vat.js`. `withVat` used `Math.floor`, which always rounds down, but the comment and the failing test both say the result should be rounded to the nearest penny. For `999` pence, `999 * 1.2` is 1198.8, so floor returned 1198 instead of 1199. I changed it to `Math.round`. I left the test as it was, since its expectations match the documented behaviour.\n\nI haven't committed the change.",
